WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.534
- But it was an unexpected kind of hazard

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.900
of that job, right.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.860
- So you're in a small confined space.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.280
The ring is 20 feet by 20 feet.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.790
And you're with a group of guys

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.503
so you always want to
try to smell your best.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:17.050
But here's the thing, we are
a global touring company.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.950
So we'll do a show in Shanghai

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.630
and then come back to San Francisco,

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:21.870
and do a show in San Francisco.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:22.910
And a lot of times,

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.180
and you know this from
being a touring musician,

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.670
sometimes travel gets messed up.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.070
Sometimes flights get
delayed, so you can like--

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:29.903
- [Kelly] No sleep.

00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:31.610
- Connect in Budapest,
land in San Francisco

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.286
and have to go to the ring in two minutes.

00:00:33.286 --> 00:00:35.340
So everybody's given a few mulligans

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.810
in the B.O. and the breath category

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:41.310
but we also have a nice
form of policing ourselves

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.300
where somebody has a few more
mulligans than they should,

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.267
we kind of give them the old,

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:48.660
"Hey man, it's our office out
there. Could you kind of--"

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.710
- Keep it together.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.240
- Yes exactly, exactly, exactly.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.420
- So was your smell kind
of a secret strategy?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.622
Did you ever smell on purpose
just to throw people off?

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.693
Give 'em the armpit kind of thing.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.490
- Actually, that's a decent...

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.020
All these years I've been
punching my way out of trouble

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.090
when I could've just smelled really bad.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.620
- [Kelly] Could've used B.O.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.010
- Man, where were you?

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.795
No, my thing was always Tic-Tacs.

00:01:10.795 --> 00:01:13.040
It's a nervous superstition

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.370
that I always have before
we go on a broadcast.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:16.830
And I've had to ween myself off of them

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.050
'cause I would up to them
like three boxes a day.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.197
And it's right in the 20
minutes before broadcast.

00:01:21.197 --> 00:01:22.030
- (gasps) That's like a child.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.718
- Yeah, it's pretty much 10,000
calories in straight sugar.

00:01:24.718 --> 00:01:27.011
- Oh my gosh, and you know what,

00:01:27.011 --> 00:01:29.680
you probably don't gain
a pound, do you John?

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.847
- Well, I have to go out there

00:01:31.847 --> 00:01:33.508
and get beat up as you saw by the photo,

00:01:33.508 --> 00:01:34.520
I don't really do well.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.700
- Okay, you've taught me something.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.003
I need to go get beat up
instead of working out.

